<!doctype html>
<html lang="en" data-skill="ui-design" data-skill-version="0.2">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="skill-name" content="UI Design">
  <meta name="skill-description" content="Visual UI design knowledge, references, rules, and examples for AI agents.">
  <title>UI Design Skill</title>
  <style>
    body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 900px; margin: 48px auto; padding: 0 24px; }
    img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>UI Design</h1>
    <p>Visual design knowledge that can be searched entry by entry.</p>
  </header>

  <section data-skill-entry data-type="instruction" data-tags="loader retrieval context">
    <h2>How to use this skill</h2>
    <p data-rule>Search tags and entries first. Load only knowledge relevant to the current task.</p>
    <p data-rule>Inspect linked visual references when they help answer the task.</p>
  </section>

  <section data-skill-entry data-type="component" data-tags="button primary action hierarchy">
    <h2>Primary button</h2>
    <p data-rule>Use the primary style for the main action. Avoid multiple competing primary actions in one focused view.</p>
    <pre data-code>&lt;button class="primary"&gt;Continue&lt;/button&gt;</pre>
  </section>

  <section data-skill-entry data-type="layout" data-tags="dashboard layout hierarchy spacing">
    <h2>Dashboard</h2>
    <p data-rule>Keep navigation stable, place the page title near the top, group related controls, and use spacing before adding borders.</p>
  </section>

  <section data-skill-entry data-type="reference" data-tags="image visual reference dashboard">
    <h2>Visual references</h2>
    <p data-rule>Store images in assets/ and reference them with normal relative HTML paths.</p>
    <img src="assets/example-ui.png" alt="Example UI reference for hierarchy and spacing">
  </section>
</body>
</html>
